I felt like you many years ago, especially as I faintly seem to
remember that there once wasn't even a "displace" feature, which
made it even more tedious with the pet between your legs blocking
your progress.

But contrary to the (up to now) prevalent opinion in this thread
I learned that pets are extreemly useful _even until the endgame_.

Monsters get tougher, and pets get tougher; you can't expect with
any character role that you can at some point handle every monster.
And pets reduce the risk that you die even if you're tough enough
but are inattentive. And, most important, they are a shield!  Two
pets in a corridor and only very few monster types can come close.
Get a horde of pets and you are surrounded by a living shield even
in any open area.

At some time in the game you're likely to find a magic whistle;
that's the point when you should consider to use a zoo of pets to
your advance. (And there are also helpful leashes to control them.)

